@heading DCS Fuel Planner - Container Diagram
@caption How the mission designer plans fuel across legs, validated against airframe capability
@legend true

[Mission Designer|Person|Builds the DCS mission fuel plan]

{Fuel Planner
[Fuel Planner SPA|Container|Airframe selector, leg builder, mission timeline, results dashboard :browser:]
[Fuel Calculation Engine|Container|Applies each leg's fuel strategy and computes cumulative burn]
[Validation Engine|Container|Runs pluggable rules: Bingo, AAR placement, leg sequence, capability]
[Leg Library|Container|Predefined legs tagged with required airframe capabilities :database:]
[Airframe Profiles|Container|Fuel flow rates, capacity, bingo/joker thresholds per airframe :database:]
[Persistence Layer|Container|Coordinates autosave and export/import]
}

[Browser Storage|Container|localStorage/IndexedDB autosave cache :database:]
[JSON Mission Files|Container|Portable, shareable mission export files]
[DCS Mission Editor|External|Manual cross-reference with DCS mission, no direct integration]

[Mission Designer]-Builds mission in->[Fuel Planner SPA]
[Fuel Planner SPA]-Sends leg sequence->[Fuel Calculation Engine]
[Fuel Calculation Engine]-Reads flow rates & thresholds->[Airframe Profiles]
[Fuel Calculation Engine]-Passes fuel state array->[Validation Engine]
[Fuel Planner SPA]-Pulls legs filtered by capability->[Leg Library]
[Fuel Planner SPA]-Autosave / load->[Persistence Layer]
[Persistence Layer]-Writes and reads-.->[Browser Storage]
[Persistence Layer]-Export / import-.->[JSON Mission Files]
[Mission Designer]-Shares file with-.->[JSON Mission Files]
[Mission Designer]-Cross references geometry-.->[DCS Mission Editor]

